WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.200
-Right now, today is Friday,
and that's usually when

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.367
I catch up
on some personal stuff.

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:05.734
I check my in-box,
I return some e-mails,

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:07.167
and I, of course,
send out thank-you notes.

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:08.400
And I was running a bit behind.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.734
Can I write out some
thank-you notes right now?

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:11.534
Is that okay with you guys?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:13.534
Thank you! I appreciate that.

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:14.667
James, can I get some

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:16.100
thank-you-note-writing music,
please?

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.534
[ Soft music playing ]

00:00:17.534 --> 00:00:21.267
Eh, how about
something different?

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:23.868
[ Up-beat music playing ]

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:26.734
[ Rhythmic clapping ]

00:00:26.734 --> 00:00:30.000
♪ I wanna say thank you ♪

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.767
♪ I wanna say thank you, now ♪

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:36.234
♪ I wanna say thank you ♪

00:00:36.234 --> 00:00:37.334
♪ Thank you ♪

00:00:37.334 --> 00:00:40.133
♪ I wanna say thank you,
now, now ♪

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:42.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:46.501
[ Soft music playing ]

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:49.501
Thank You, nutcrackers,
for always looking like

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:51.968
you just saw what Kanye posted.

00:00:53.968 --> 00:00:55.767
-Ay-yi-yi!

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:57.434
What?!

00:00:58.567 --> 00:00:59.868
[ Soft music playing ]

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:02.501
-Thank you, restaurants whose
specials today are

00:01:02.501 --> 00:01:05.300
cranberry Turkey,
for making it pretty obvious

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:06.634
this food is a week old.

00:01:06.634 --> 00:01:09.501
It's like,
"That's cranberry turkey?"

00:01:12.734 --> 00:01:13.801
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:15.868
Thank you, mistletoe,

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:18.868
for being the most festive way
to get cancelled.

00:01:23.868 --> 00:01:25.267
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:28.367
Thank you, Spotify Wrapped,
or, as you're also known,

00:01:28.367 --> 00:01:31.067
"Spotify: Taylor's Version."

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:33.968
She crushed it.

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:35.968
She crushed it.

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:37.634
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:40.701
Thank you, the morning
after black Friday,

00:01:40.701 --> 00:01:42.000
for being the moment
I wake up next to

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.100
a new flat-screen TV like,
"Wait, did we..."

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:53.033
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:55.267
Thank you, real Christmas trees,

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:57.567
for being so excited
to come home, relax,

00:01:57.567 --> 00:01:58.634
and take off your Spanx.

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:03.501
Just relax.

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:06.701
[ Soft music playing ]

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:08.968
Thank you,
Christmas craft fairs,

00:02:08.968 --> 00:02:11.234
for being a fun, festive way
to walk around

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:14.400
dozens of little shops
and going, "Eh."

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:19.234
"Do we need this?"

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:20.234
-No, I'm good.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.834
[ Soft music playing ]

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:25.934
Thank you, poinsettias,

00:02:25.934 --> 00:02:27.701
for being the
po-tay-to/po-tah-to

00:02:27.701 --> 00:02:28.868
of Christmas.

00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:32.067
Is it "poinsettas,
poinsettas, poinsettas"?

00:02:32.067 --> 00:02:33.434
Poinsettias?

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:36.467
[ Soft music playing ]

00:02:36.467 --> 00:02:38.567
Thank you,
Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer,

00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:39.734
for teaching children

00:02:39.734 --> 00:02:41.367
that it doesn't matter
if you're different.

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:43.934
What matters is that
you're useful once a year.

00:02:43.934 --> 00:02:45.968
There you have it, everybody.
Those are our "Thank You Notes."

